  "live_records": {
    "q-110256": {
      "dom_id": "step-q110256",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "A seller delivers bricks on pallets. One pallet contains $500$ bricks. The weight of a brick is normally distributed with a mean of $3\\,\\text{lb}$ and a standard deviation of $0.25\\,\\text{lb},$ while the weight of a pallet is normally distributed with a mean of $40\\,\\text{lb}$ and a standard deviation of $4\\,\\text{lb}.$ If one pallet with bricks is randomly selected, what is the probability that it weighs less than $1\\,545\\,\\text{lb}?$ You may assume that the weights are independent.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.7324\\,$ | $\\,0.7357\\,$ | $\\,0.7389\\,$ | $\\,0.7422\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7642\\,$ | $\\,0.7673\\,$ | $\\,0.7704\\,$ | $\\,0.7734\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.7939\\,$ | $\\,0.7967\\,$ | $\\,0.7995\\,$ | $\\,0.8023\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Let ${X}_{i}$ denote the weight of the $i$th brick, and let $Y$ denote the weight of a pallet. Then, we have\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}∼N(3,{0.25}^{2}),\\,1\\le i\\le 500,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nY∼N(40,{4}^{2}).\n$$\n\nLet the random variable $W$ denote the weight of a randomly selected pallet with bricks. Then, since\n\n$$\nW={X}_{1}+{X}_{2}+⋯+{X}_{500}+Y,\n$$\n\nwe have that $W$ is normally distributed, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[W] & =500\\cdot 3+40 \\\\  & =1\\,540, \\\\ \\text{Var}[W] & =500\\cdot {0.25}^{2}+{4}^{2} \\\\  & =47.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nW∼N(1\\,540,47.25).\n$$\n\nIn order to find $P(W<1\\,545),$ we convert $W$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(W<1\\,545) & =P(Z<\\frac{1\\,545-1\\,540}{\\sqrt{47.25}}) \\\\  & ≈P(Z<0.73) \\\\  & =Φ(0.73)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the $z$-table, we see that\n\n$$\nΦ(0.73)≈0.7673.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(W<1\\,545) & ≈Φ(0.73) \\\\  & ≈0.7673.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
