      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Given that ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{20}$ are I.I.D random variables, where\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}∼N(1,{2}^{2}),\\,1\\le i\\le 20,\n$$\n\nwhat is the distribution of $Y={X}_{1}+{X}_{2}+⋯+{X}_{20}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{20}$ are independent and identically distributed (I.I.D) normal random variables, where \n\n$$\n{X}_{i}∼N(\\mu ,{\\sigma }^{2}),\\,1\\le i\\le n,\n$$\n\nthen \n\n$$\nY={X}_{1}+{X}_{2}+⋯+{X}_{n}∼N(n\\mu ,\\,n{\\sigma }^{2}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, since ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{20}$ are mutually independent, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y={X}_{1}+{X}_{2}+⋯+{X}_{20} & ∼N(20\\cdot 1,\\,20\\cdot {2}^{2}) \\\\  & ∼N(20\\cdot 1,\\,20\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =N(20,80).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
